---
description: Operating rules for the Neural Wind Tunnel repository
alwaysApply: true
---

Follow `AGENTS.md` in the repository root. It is the full manual: commands, conventions, git
workflow and the autonomous loop.

Work through `docs/PLAN.md` in order, starting at the first unticked task. Do not skip ahead and
do not widen a task into a refactor of its neighbours.

After every task: run `pnpm lint typecheck test build` plus `pnpm test:e2e` for visual work and
`uv run ruff check . && uv run pytest` for Python work, verify the task's acceptance criteria
yourself, commit with a Conventional Commit message, push, tick the checkbox in `docs/PLAN.md`,
and append an entry to `docs/PROGRESS.md`.

Hard rules:

- Commit messages contain no co-author trailers and no mention of the tool that wrote them.
- Never commit secrets, datasets, model artifacts or binaries over a megabyte.
- Never force-push and never rewrite pushed history.
- The velocity field is always reconstructed from the model's predicted POD coefficients.
  Procedural noise never substitutes for a solution.
- Every accuracy or performance number in any document is measured, reproducible and honest,
  including when a target was missed.
- `docs/DATASET-SCHEMA.md` and `docs/URL-STATE.md` are contracts shared with a sister
  repository. Changing one is deliberate, versioned and recorded in `CHANGELOG.md`.
- Running unattended, never stop to ask. Choose a default, add an ADR to `docs/DECISIONS.md`,
  note it in `docs/QUESTIONS.md`, continue.
